  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "Negotiation Mental Model",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 0,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Negotiation Mental Model",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What Negotiation Is",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Client states what it can handle; ==server picks== a representation",
                "**One URL**, many formats of the same resource"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. The Three Headers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Header",
                "Direction",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Accept`",
                  "request",
                  "formats I want back"
                ],
                [
                  "`Accept-Encoding`",
                  "request",
                  "compressions I can decode"
                ],
                [
                  "`Content-Type`",
                  "request or response",
                  "format of this body"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 2
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client",
                    "sub": "Accept, Accept-Encoding",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Server",
                    "sub": "picks one",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Response",
                    "sub": "Content-Type, Vary",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Who Decides",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Server-driven== negotiation is the norm",
                "Send `Vary: Accept` and `Vary: Accept-Encoding`",
                "Vary makes caches key on those headers"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Top header bug",
              "text": "`Content-Type` describes the body in **this** message; `Accept` describes the preferred response."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Accept vs Content-Type?** Accept = response I want; Content-Type = format of this body",
                "**Who decides?** The server, from the client's Accept list",
                "**Why Vary?** Caches key on it, or serve the wrong format"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Media Types and Accept Rules",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 1,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Media Types and Accept Rules",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Media Type Syntax",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Form: `type/subtype;param`",
                "`application/json`, `image/png`, `text/html;charset=utf-8`",
                "Vendor type: `application/vnd.company.v2+json`",
                "`+json` suffix = the structure is ==JSON==",
                "Used for ==versioning== and custom schemas"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Accept and q-values",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "Accept: application/json, text/html;q=0.8, */*;q=0.1"
              ],
              "note": "q runs 0 to 1, default 1"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Specificity (equal q)",
                "Match"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Wins",
                  "`application/json`"
                ],
                [
                  "Then",
                  "`application/*`"
                ],
                [
                  "Last",
                  "`*/*`"
                ]
              ],
              "highlightRow": 0
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Charset Rule",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`application/json` is always ==UTF-8==: omit `;charset=utf-8`",
                "`text/*` types: include `;charset=utf-8`"
              ],
              "style": "check",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Tie rule",
              "text": "Higher q wins. On equal q, the ==more specific== type wins over wildcards."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**How do q-values resolve a tie?** Equal q: the most specific type wins",
                "**What does +json mean?** The body structure is JSON",
                "**Version by media type?** Keep one URL; clients pick the version with Accept"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "ink": "orange"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "406, 415 and Choosing Formats",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 2,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "406, 415 and Choosing Formats",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. 406 vs 415",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "",
                "406",
                "415"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "Means",
                  "Not Acceptable",
                  "Unsupported Media Type"
                ],
                [
                  "About",
                  "response format",
                  "request body format"
                ],
                [
                  "Header",
                  "`Accept`",
                  "`Content-Type`"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flowchart",
              "spec": {
                "rows": [
                  [
                    "q1",
                    "a"
                  ],
                  [
                    "q2",
                    "b"
                  ],
                  [
                    "ok"
                  ]
                ],
                "nodes": {
                  "q1": {
                    "text": "Content-Type readable?",
                    "shape": "diamond"
                  },
                  "a": {
                    "text": "415",
                    "shape": "box",
                    "ink": "red"
                  },
                  "q2": {
                    "text": "Accept satisfiable?",
                    "shape": "diamond"
                  },
                  "b": {
                    "text": "406 or default JSON",
                    "shape": "box",
                    "ink": "orange"
                  },
                  "ok": {
                    "text": "200",
                    "shape": "pill",
                    "ink": "green"
                  }
                },
                "edges": [
                  {
                    "from": "q1",
                    "to": "a",
                    "label": "no"
                  },
                  {
                    "from": "q1",
                    "to": "q2",
                    "label": "yes"
                  },
                  {
                    "from": "q2",
                    "to": "b",
                    "label": "no"
                  },
                  {
                    "from": "q2",
                    "to": "ok",
                    "label": "yes"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Missing or wrong ==Content-Type== on POST → usually **415**",
                "Many APIs ignore a bad `Accept` and return default JSON",
                "Both allowed: ==pick one==, document it"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Quick memory",
              "text": "406 = I can't **give** you that. 415 = I can't **take** that."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Choosing a format",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Format",
                "Use"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "JSON",
                  "API default: universal, readable"
                ],
                [
                  "XML",
                  "legacy, SOAP"
                ],
                [
                  "Protobuf / MessagePack",
                  "compact binary"
                ],
                [
                  "CSV",
                  "tabular export"
                ],
                [
                  "`multipart/form-data`",
                  "file uploads"
                ],
                [
                  "`application/x-www-form-urlencoded`",
                  "simple forms"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**406 vs 415?** 406: Accept unmet. 415: request Content-Type unreadable",
                "**POST JSON gives 415?** Content-Type missing or not `application/json`",
                "**Protobuf over JSON?** Compact, fast, typed service-to-service traffic"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Compression with Accept-Encoding",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 3,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Compression with Accept-Encoding",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Request and Response",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "diagram",
              "kind": "flow",
              "spec": {
                "nodes": [
                  {
                    "text": "Client",
                    "sub": "Accept-Encoding: gzip, br, zstd",
                    "ink": "blue"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Server picks",
                    "sub": "gzip",
                    "ink": "green"
                  },
                  {
                    "text": "Reply",
                    "sub": "Content-Encoding: gzip + Vary: Accept-Encoding",
                    "ink": "purple"
                  }
                ]
              }
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Content-Encoding== = compression of the body",
                "==Content-Type== stays the original: `application/json`, not `application/gzip`"
              ],
              "style": "dot",
              "frame": "dashed",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Which Codec, Which Bodies",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Codec",
                "Strength",
                "Note"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "**gzip**",
                  "universal default",
                  "works everywhere"
                ],
                [
                  "**br** (Brotli)",
                  "best ratio for text",
                  "slow to compress; static assets"
                ],
                [
                  "**zstd**",
                  "fast, good ratio",
                  "newer support"
                ]
              ],
              "frame": "dashed"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "{green:Compress} text: JSON, HTML, CSS, JS, XML",
                "{red:Skip} JPEG, PNG, MP4, ZIP: already compressed",
                "{red:Skip} tiny bodies under about ==1 KB=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Test, Risk, Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "bash",
              "lines": [
                "curl --compressed -i https://api.example.com/items",
                "curl -H 'Accept-Encoding: gzip' --output - https://api.example.com/items"
              ],
              "note": "second form shows the raw compressed bytes"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "BREACH",
              "text": "Do not compress responses that mix **secrets** with attacker-controlled input over TLS."
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**Which header says how it compressed?** `Content-Encoding`",
                "**Why not compress images?** Already compressed; CPU wasted",
                "**Why Vary: Accept-Encoding?** Caches keep one copy per encoding"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Problem Details (RFC 9457) Errors",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 4,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Problem Details (RFC 9457) Errors",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. What It Is",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Standard JSON error body, served as ==application/problem+json==",
                "XML variant: `application/problem+xml`",
                "Obsoletes RFC 7807"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Members",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Member",
                "Holds"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`type`",
                  "URI for the error kind, default `about:blank`"
                ],
                [
                  "`title`",
                  "short, stable summary"
                ],
                [
                  "`status`",
                  "HTTP code"
                ],
                [
                  "`detail`",
                  "this occurrence, human-readable"
                ],
                [
                  "`instance`",
                  "URI of this occurrence"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "json",
              "lines": [
                "{",
                "  \"type\": \"https://api.example.com/errors/out-of-credit\",",
                "  \"title\": \"Out of credit\",",
                "  \"status\": 403,",
                "  \"detail\": \"Balance is 30, cost is 50.\",",
                "  \"instance\": \"/account/12345/txn/abc\"",
                "}"
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "==Extension members== add machine-readable data, e.g. `\"balance\": 30`",
                "422 validation: an `errors` array of field violations",
                "Clients must ==ignore unknown members=="
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Mistakes",
              "ink": "orange"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "`status` in the body must match the HTTP status line",
                "No stack traces or internals in `detail`"
              ],
              "style": "cross"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Branch on type",
              "text": "Switch on a ==stable `type`==; never parse `title` or `detail` for logic."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Cheat Sheet: Negotiation and Errors",
      "role": "outline",
      "outlineIndex": 5,
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Cheat Sheet: Negotiation and Errors",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "1. Headers",
              "ink": "blue"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Header",
                "Side",
                "Meaning"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "`Accept`",
                  "request",
                  "formats I want"
                ],
                [
                  "`Accept-Encoding`",
                  "request",
                  "compressions I can decode"
                ],
                [
                  "`Content-Type`",
                  "both",
                  "body I am sending"
                ],
                [
                  "`Content-Encoding`",
                  "response",
                  "compression used"
                ],
                [
                  "`Vary`",
                  "response",
                  "headers the choice depends on"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "2. Status Codes",
              "ink": "red"
            },
            {
              "type": "table",
              "headers": [
                "Status",
                "Cause"
              ],
              "rows": [
                [
                  "{red:406}",
                  "wrong `Accept`"
                ],
                [
                  "{red:415}",
                  "wrong request `Content-Type`"
                ],
                [
                  "{orange:400}",
                  "malformed body, cannot be parsed"
                ],
                [
                  "{purple:422}",
                  "parses but fails validation"
                ]
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "code",
              "lang": "http",
              "lines": [
                "Accept: application/json,",
                "  application/vnd.acme.v2+json;q=0.9,",
                "  */*;q=0.1"
              ],
              "note": "q defaults to 1; most specific wins"
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "3. Compression and Errors",
              "ink": "green"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "Compress text with ==gzip/br==; skip images and tiny payloads",
                "Always send `Vary: Accept-Encoding`",
                "Errors: `application/problem+json` with ==type, title, status, detail, instance==",
                "Add extension members for machine-readable data"
              ],
              "style": "check"
            },
            {
              "type": "callout",
              "style": "sticky",
              "title": "Remember",
              "text": "Switch on `type`, not `title`. Body `status` must match the HTTP status line."
            },
            {
              "type": "heading",
              "text": "4. Interview Point",
              "ink": "purple"
            },
            {
              "type": "bullets",
              "items": [
                "**End to end?** Send Accept + Accept-Encoding; reply Content-Type, Content-Encoding, Vary",
                "**Unsupported body type?** ==415==",
                "**Consistent errors?** One problem+json shape, stable `type` URIs, extensions"
              ],
              "style": "dot"
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Check yourself",
      "role": "quiz",
      "pages": [
        {
          "title": "Check yourself",
          "blocks": [
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A client POSTs a JSON body with `Accept: application/json` but `Content-Type: text/plain`. The API only reads JSON. What status, and why?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "**415**, because the server won't read the request body's type.",
                "`Accept` is fine, so 406 is wrong."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "A server gzips a JSON reply and sends `Content-Type: application/gzip`. What is wrong?",
              "a_bullets": [
                "`Content-Type` stays `application/json`.",
                "Compression goes in `Content-Encoding: gzip`, plus `Vary: Accept-Encoding`."
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "qa",
              "q": "An error reply has status line 400, `Content-Type: application/json` and body `{\"status\":422}`. Spot the bugs.",
              "a_bullets": [
                "Body status must match the status line.",
                "Use `application/problem+json`."
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
